       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **The order as written:** 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**.\n- **The maximum:** The maximum daily dose of metformin for adults is **2,550 mg/day**. That is usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Immediate-release metformin is typically capped at 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day.\n- **The risk:** The order is 3 times the maximum. It could cause severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nIt seems 2550 mg was meant as the total daily dose. Which of these do you want?\n\n1. **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day total).\n2. **500 mg PO three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day), or another dose that suits the patient. Metformin is usually started low, such as 500 mg once or twice daily, and increased slowly.\n3. A different dose you have confirmed with your resident or attending.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it. Please also check the plan with your supervising physician or pharmacist."
